hindsight is 20/20 and after going  through Fire Emblem three houses we  found even more things we wish we knew  before we started our tenure at Garrick  Mach monastery fair warning there are  some minor spoilers in this video but we  believe these tips are more useful  before you encounter them there are  loads of different support conversations  to be had between students and faculty  however it never gets to a point where  you can date any of them some ice rinks  have a suggestion of marriage but that's  as far as it ever goes students also  can't date each other so you can't be  playing matchmaker either fishing  doesn't cost any activity points and it  increases your professor level making it  a must for every Sunday you decide to  explore the monastery on some Sundays  they're rare fish that can be caught and  sold for lots of cash to have a better  chance of catching these fish we  actually recommend not always going for  the first fish that grabs your line when  a fish catches on you'll see an icon in  the bottom right telling you the rarity  of the fish you'll want to wait for the  purple gold or rainbow fish icon to  appear be careful though there's a risk  of losing your line after the third try  or fourth if you're lucky  [Music]  in the month of September flame will go  missing and your mission for the month  is to find her during your time  exploring the monastery that month you  could speak with your house leader to  trigger a quest that asked you to find  clues about flames whereabouts there is  a prime suspect however if you decide to  enter their room right away you will  automatically skip to the end of  September we recommend waiting until the  end of the month before you trigger that  quest so you continue to spend activity  points and cultivate your team  battalions are extremely useful for  almost every character in the game  they provide stat buffs and allow gambit  attacks the only character you should  avoid giving a battalion to is Felix  from the blue lions as it conflicts with  his unique ability battalions do cost  money to recruit and replenish Plus what  you can equip is limited by authority  skill and whether you have a flying unit  or not so keep that in mind when  deciding who should and shouldn't get  one special merchant vendors show up  after you clear certain battles once  they do arrive at Garrick Mach it's a  good idea to buy as many presents as you  can from them as they'll give more  motivation than ordinary presents  depending on who you give them to  sharing meals can cover a lot of your  students motivation already but as you  expand into recruiting more students and  characters this can become an effective  way to increase motivation and social  rank for more people in one day  each month you can have one student from  another house assist your team in  battles for that month this can be  extremely useful as you'll have one  extra person on the team and they can  help balance out a weak spot your team  might have this can also help build your  bonds with that character if you're  looking to potentially recruit them  however that character won't receive any  experience and you'll be taking away  experience you could be giving to one of  your own units  [Applause]  on top of lost items sometimes you'll  find guides for cooking or fishing just  lying around grabbing these will  increase your professor level at no cost  despite its ethical implications don't  be shy about entering the rooms of your  students and other professors in order  to grab some of these basically just  pick up any glowing blue object you see  on the ground and we suggest looking  around for more every time you enter a  new month occasionally you'll pick up  rusted weapons on the battlefield this  will happen more often if you're  connected online and land on squares  that are glowing purple don't  immediately throw them away however  instead you should inspect them with X  on the inventory screen to see if the  rusted weapon has the potential to  become a grater if you forge them with  the blacksmith well some could simply go  from rusted to iron others can be forged  into uniquely named weapons which are  super rare just a heads up the  blacksmith isn't available until a few  months in and you need to complete a  side quest to open it  didn't quite get all the characters up  to their highest support level or just  want to see how a different house  unfolds after you complete the game  there's a new game plus mode first of  all it doesn't wipe your main save data  so you're good after that you'll retain  shop levels and statue perks but you can  now spend renowned on a number of things  to put you back at the levels you were  at in your original file this includes  your professor level the skills of the  professor and the students and the  support levels between characters you  don't have all the renowned in the world  though so it's important to choose what  you want to regain faster  this one is more of a fun little easter  egg than it is a tip have you ever  noticed that the little sprite avatar on  the loading screen is moving well you  can actually control which direction  they move and how fast they're moving  it's all in the gyro controls so that  means tilting your controller or tilting  the system itself if you're in handheld  mode you can also hit B to jump and a to  flip their cape those are just a few  more things we wish we knew in Fire  Emblem three houses if you haven't seen  our first video about nine things we  wish we knew you should definitely give  it a watch anything you found that's  been helpful in your playthrough leave  it down in the comments and thanks for  watching  [Music]
 

